From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 13:46:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Allow up to 32 compute units with a
 shared UMA pool

Every compute command in flight holds one compute unit until the host
retires it, so the unit count is the depth of the compute queue. Each
unit carries a 32 MiB UMA pool at its own place in the client address
range, and the fixed layout has room for 16 such units. The 25G83
layout has 32 compute UMA slots, though.

With g16_compute_shared_pool, every unit already allocates from unit
0's pool, so in that mode the units after the first no longer get a
pool, state and page list of their own: they take unit 0's, and keep
only what is theirs per command, a work page, the preemption and
auxiliary buffers and a context store (about 300 KiB). Let
g16_compute_units go up to 32 in that mode; units 16 to 31 get 512 KiB
of address range each, between the compute work pages and compute
unit 0. Without the shared pool nothing changes and the limit stays 16.

Size the per-unit tables, the lifetime ledger and the flight capacity
for 32 units, keep the render paths at their own unit count, and keep
the slot tables in a box of their own so that they stay off the probe
path's stack. The default of 12 units is unchanged.

Assisted-by: LLM
